      "id": 1,
      "text": "James Murphy, manager of the Holt estate, christened the suburb Miranda after the Shakespearean heroine from The Tempest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miranda%2C_New_South_Wales",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The suburb’s layout was crafted in the 1950s by architects Lipson & Kadd, who also designed the nearby Padstow Hotel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miranda%2C_New_South_Wales",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Miranda Library opened its doors in 1955, becoming the first public library in the Sutherland Shire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miranda%2C_New_South_Wales",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The five‑way roundabout at The Boulevard, Kiora Road and Port Hacking Road was replaced by traffic lights in 2002, dropping collisions from 222 to 13 the next year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miranda%2C_New_South_Wales",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early settlers, drawn by fertile land, established poultry farms and market gardens on what is now Miranda, with John Connell’s 1816 selection forming the suburb’s core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://localhistory.sutherlandshire.nsw.gov.au/nodes/view/6089",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Miranda railway station, on the Cronulla branch of the Illawarra line, links the suburb directly to Sydney’s City Circle, making a quick trip to the CBD possible.",
